From a1cad7bef12d3139e231cb655626c128d5f97aae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:18:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/15] Fix remaining big-endian gaps and an uninitialised
 Blitz in generic code

- ide/Builders: give struct Blitz default initialisers. GccBuilder leaves
  it unassigned for noblitz packages (ide/Builders, plugin/pcre); with
  gcc16 the BLITZ step then ran on stack garbage: a compiler invocation
  with empty input and output names and a garbage file count in the log.
- Core/String.h: make the chr[KIND] mask in String0::IsEqual a compile
  time constant. The function-local static added a guard check to one
  of the hottest inline functions.
- plugin/bmp: BI_BITFIELDS masks are little-endian on disk, read and
  write them with Peek32le/Poke32le; swap the header before validating
  biSize; swap the header written by WriteIcon.
- Draw/RasterFormat.cpp: the "source is already BGRA" shortcuts copy
  source bytes straight into RGBA. RGBA is { a, r, g, b } in MacOS, so
  disable them there, like RasterWrite.cpp already does.
- Draw/Drawing.cpp: byte-swap the legacy 16-bit text run on big-endian.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
